{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Context / Problem\n\nMeasurement 50e3-6d2a-0e7f-4e92 found the recorded caused_by edges cannot be partitioned into\nblame-derived guesses vs explicitly supplied attributions: `_apply_caused_by`\n(src/rebar/_commands/transition_close.py) writes both origins through `_write_link_event` with\nno provenance field, so on read a guessed edge is indistinguishable from a proven one and the\nescaped-defect consumers (`rebar metrics` bug_trends lens, the epic-close caused_by floor)\nweight them identically. The operator accepted this proposal — see the OPERATOR DECISION\ncomment on this ticket — so this ticket now implements the marker. It builds directly on the\nmerged caused_by target validation (change 2125, ticket 77e7-1eec-7b52-46ed).\n\n## Approach\n\nAdd an OPTIONAL `provenance` field to the caused_by LINK event payload, value `\"derived\"`\n(blame auto-derivation) or `\"explicit\"` (operator/agent-supplied). Old events carry no field\nand read as unknown — no migration is needed: the dep schema (`common.schema.json` `$defs/dep`)\nalready allows additional properties, and the reducer surfaces the field present-only (the\nsame pattern as the comment `source_*` provenance fields).\n\n- `rebar.graph._links._write_link_event` gains an optional `provenance` parameter, included in\n  the LINK event data only when set.\n- `transition_close._apply_caused_by` passes `\"explicit\"` when the close carried a non-empty\n  `--caused-by`, `\"derived\"` when the culprit came from `blame.derive_caused_by`. No change to\n  the deriver's fail-closed behaviour (the strict-majority abstention stays as designed).\n- `add_dependency` (the `rebar link` path shared by CLI/library/MCP) marks caused_by writes\n  `\"explicit\"` — a linked attribution is supplied by the caller, never blame-derived. Other\n  relations are unchanged (no field written).\n- `reducer/_processors.py process_link` copies `provenance` onto the dep entry present-only,\n  so replay of old unmarked events yields the exact prior dep shape.\n- `common.schema.json` documents the optional enum on the dep def.\n- `rebar metrics`: bug_trends rows carry per-edge provenance and a new STOCK dimension\n  `bug_caused_by_provenance` reports the explicit/derived/unknown edge counts, so escape-rate\n  consumers can weight proven attributions above guessed ones. `bug_caused_by_fan_in` keeps\n  its existing shape.\n\n## Scope\n\n- src/rebar/graph/_links.py — `_write_link_event` provenance param; `add_dependency` marks\n  caused_by explicit.\n- src/rebar/_commands/transition_close.py — `_apply_caused_by` selects derived vs explicit.\n- src/rebar/reducer/_processors.py — `process_link` surfaces the field present-only.\n- src/rebar/schemas/common.schema.json — optional `provenance` property on the dep def.\n- src/rebar/metrics/bug_trends.py — per-edge provenance in rows + the\n  `bug_caused_by_provenance` dimension.\n- docs/event-schema.md, docs/user-guide.md — document the marker and the new dimension.\n- tests/unit/test_caused_by_provenance.py (new) — write-site and replay coverage.\n- tests/unit/metrics/test_bug_trends.py — the new dimension's derivation.\n\n## Testing\n\nUnit tests, written RED-first: (1) a bug close with an EMPTY `--caused-by` and a stubbed blame\nculprit writes the edge with provenance `\"derived\"`; (2) a close with an explicit `--caused-by`\nwrites `\"explicit\"`; (3) `rebar link <bug> <origin> caused_by` writes `\"explicit\"`;\n(4) legacy/failure path — replay of a pre-marker LINK event (no field) reduces to a dep entry\nWITHOUT a provenance key (shape unchanged, reduction succeeds), and blame returning no culprit\nstill writes nothing; (5) `bug_caused_by_provenance` counts explicit/derived/unknown edges and\nreturns None when no caused_by edges exist (the unavailable/empty path).\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [x] Both transition_close write origins populate the marker: unit tests assert `\"derived\"`\n      on the blame path and `\"explicit\"` on the `--caused-by` path.\n- [x] `rebar link … caused_by` marks `\"explicit\"`: unit test asserts the dep entry's field.\n- [x] Old unmarked events read as unknown: a replay unit test shows the dep entry carries no\n      provenance key and reduction succeeds unchanged.\n- [x] `rebar metrics` distinguishes supplied vs derived edges: the bug_trends lens gains\n      `bug_caused_by_provenance` with explicit/derived/unknown counts, asserted by unit test.\n- [x] docs/event-schema.md documents the marker and docs/user-guide.md lists the new\n      dimension: verified by reading the landed diff."}},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1787452987080858001,"uuid":"a512c197-a19e-4504-b9df-c7fc68ec4794"}